# Test Intent: MultiPageJourney

Site: nordbank
Requested by: monitoring team
Date: 2026-07-13

## Target URL

Open the file `journey/index.html` — the Nordbank landing page shipped in this
workspace (the fake online-banking start page).

## Desired Flow

I opened the Nordbank landing page. It is a busy marketing homepage with a big
hero banner, lots of promo tiles, a main navigation bar, and a cluttered footer.
There is NO login form on this first page.

To reach online banking I had to look carefully: up in the small links at the
very top-right, among "Private", "Business", "Help", "Contact" and others, there
is one link labelled "Online Banking". I clicked it.

That took me to an "Online Banking" information page — more marketing, feature
promos, and several calls to action ("Register now", "Download the app", "System
status"). The step that actually leads to the login is not a big button; it is a
promo link that reads "Sign in to your account". I clicked that.

Now I was on the login wall: a username field and a password field. I typed the
demo username and the demo password, then clicked "Sign in".

I landed on my accounts dashboard. It shows my account name, my IBAN, and my
available balance, plus a "Last login" timestamp near the bottom.

## Element Hints

- The "Online Banking" entry is one link among many in the top utility bar
  (top-right). It is easy to miss.
- On the interstitial page, the link that leads to the login reads
  "Sign in to your account" and is styled like an ordinary promo link, not a
  prominent button.
- The demo credentials are username `demo` and password `Passw0rd!` (carried in
  the package `.env` as DEMO_USER / DEMO_PASS).

## Values to Capture

- The available balance shown on the dashboard, in EUR (e.g. "4250.00").

## Success Criteria

I am signed in and looking at the accounts dashboard. I can see the account name
"Demo Checking Account", the IBAN, and an available balance that is a number
greater than zero. The "Last login" time is shown but, because it changes every
visit, it must NOT be checked for a specific value.

